  "MERMAID.TAG": "Tag",
  "HELP.CORE": "# Markian\n\n## Keyboard\n\n- Ctrl/Cmd+Z: Undo\n- Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Z: Redo\n- Ctrl/Cmd+S: Request host save\n\n## Source\n\nSource preserves unsupported Markdown. Back restores the previous task.\n",
  "HELP.CODE": "\n## Code blocks\n\nExpand a fenced block to edit its complete literal source. Back applies text and language changes as one document undo step. Undo/Redo and indentation affect the local draft; saved Markdown includes the draft before Back. The Code language menu chooses highlighting without translating source. Tab indents using the configured width; Shift+Tab outdents. Press Escape then Tab to leave Tab handling. Unknown, failed, or oversized highlighting retains plain editable source. Retry highlighting retries failed assets.\n",
  "HELP.MERMAID": "\n## Mermaid diagrams\n\nUse Insert diagram or Edit diagram to open the code/preview workspace. Diagram type replaces the current source with a Class, Flowchart, Sequence, State, Use case, ERD, or Git graph template; Undo restores it. Use case uses ordinary flowchart syntax. The left sidebar follows the source declaration and inserts literal snippets at the cursor or replaces selected text. Edit example names and hex colors in source; add line breaks where needed. Git graph offers commits, branches and comments, not unsupported shape/color controls. Unsupported declarations keep source and offer comments only.\n\nBack applies the draft as one document edit. Source drafts are included in saved Markdown before Back. Undo/redo and indentation affect the diagram session. Press Escape then Tab to leave source Tab handling. Diagram arrow keys pan, plus/minus zoom, and Home resets; pointer dragging and zoom buttons also work when read-only. Syntax errors retain the ordinary Mermaid fence.\n"
}
